PCMCIA drivers supplied with AmiNetXDuo
======================================

These are unmodified, independently loaded SANA-II drivers by Neil Cafferkey.
They are not linked into AmiNetXDuo. Only a selected card's missing driver
and pccard.library are installed; existing copies are preserved.

  prism2.device 2.9: Prism II / Hermes wireless PCMCIA and CF cards
  xircomce2.device 1.1: supported Xircom CreditCard Ethernet PCMCIA cards
  pccard.library 2.2: shared PCMCIA CIS parser

The driver and library binaries are GPL-2.0-or-later. Some pccard source
files are GPL-2.0-only and some developer headers have LGPL terms; their
original notices and both license texts are retained in the source archive.
WirelessManager has its separate BSD license in Wireless/.

The Hermes firmware has separate AT&T/Lucent/Agere redistribution terms,
reproduced verbatim from the Prism2 manual in Docs/Hermes-LICENSE. Keep that
notice with the firmware. Read Docs/Prism2.guide for card-specific firmware,
encryption and router compatibility; installing this driver does not update
a Prism II card's on-card firmware.

Corresponding source, build files and original notices are supplied IN THIS
DISTRIBUTION, in PCMCIA/Sources/, as the complete original upstream archives:

  prism2v2.lha  https://aminet.net/driver/net/prism2v2.lha
  xircomce2.lha https://aminet.net/driver/net/xircomce2.lha
  pccard.lha    https://aminet.net/util/libs/pccard.lha

The standalone pccard archive is necessary: the two driver archives include
its binary but not its source. Its binary matches both driver archives.
This is GPL source distribution with the binaries, not a written offer or
a requirement that recipients obtain source from a website.

SHA256.json pins every binary, original manual, license and source archive.
tools/pcmcia-drivers.py verifies the pins before staging a release and can
refetch and compare the original archives with --fetch. No network fetch is
needed to build a distribution. Source archives stay in the unpacked release;
they are not copied to the Amiga's system directories or loaded into RAM.
